seg-5853aaba827f = The thread converts at the handover, never inside a phase, and each conversion is its own budget row. Frames: GCRF, MCI, MCMF (ITRF and LVLH are refused with the reason). <c1/> shifts the origin by the Moon's geocentric state: the DE440-grade state from the kernel where it covers the epoch (stand-in { "5" } m and { "1" } mm/s; measured worst { "2.6" } m against pinned JPL Horizons), otherwise the analytic series with its measured { "195.7" } km RMS, which the row states; a lunar example must therefore carry a kernel covering its epoch. <c2/> is the mean sidereal rotation with the axes aligned at the epoch and no libration. Timescales go through TT: <c3/> exact, <c4/> adds { "14" } us, <c5/> uses the secular rate of <c6/> with its { "56" } to { "59" } us/day band as the rate uncertainty.

