seg-d16877f38793 = The budget carries the <b>relative</b> sigmas; the chaser's absolute covariance is handed on unchanged and a row says so, because this phase measures the vehicles against each other, not against the Earth. The starting relative covariance is the chaser's absolute one plus the target's stated sigmas, added as if independent (conservative). Keys: <c1/>, <c2/>, <c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/>, optional <c6/> and <c7/>, and one or more <c8/> with <c9/>, <c10/>, <c11/>, <c12/> (<c13/>, <c14/> or <c15/>, ILLUSTRATIVE parameters in <c16/>) and <c17/>; the legs' durations add to the phase's. The docking window is the time from which the relative sigma stays inside the capture envelope to the end of the phase. Repeats are separate phases with their own ids.

# text
# c1: step_s
seg-088b78574ab4 = The mean state is the engine's Cowell propagator with Earth gravity and J2 and the Sun and Moon as third bodies. The covariance goes through each <c1/> segment with a forward-difference state-transition matrix (the nominal run and six perturbed runs) and a white acceleration noise. The burn is along the entry velocity with a stated size fraction and pointing error. <b>Limit named:</b> the committed Moon kernel cuts hold the Moon but not the Sun, so the propagator takes the Moon from the kernel and the Sun from the analytic series (the Sun's third-body term is insensitive to that series' error); the phase says which it used in an event, and where no kernel covers a segment it uses the analytic series for both. The burn is <b>not targeted</b>: the nominal state is wherever the stated burn goes, and the lunar phases take only the covariance.

