seg-3a69ca6723ba = The coast is the <c1/> coast with no burn, ending at the entry interface; its keys are the coast keys above. At the interface the phase reads the flight-path angle and its sigma from the full covariance, the probability that the angle is inside a stated corridor, the peak deceleration at the nominal angle and at both corridor edges (the engine's planar ballistic entry beside the Allen-Eggers closed form) against an optional limit, and the footprint: downrange from a stated sensitivity, crossrange from the interface covariance across the orbit plane. Keys: <c2/>, <c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/>, <c6/>, <c7/>, optional <c8/>, <c9/> and <c10/> (the nominal return state, six numbers, when the chain has no trans-Earth burn to produce one). Nothing here models a capsule's lift, guidance or heating.

