seg-69d6ab8e93bc = An optional <c1/> table gives stations and the lowest tracking elevation; for each phase it names, the thread computes the fraction of the phase a station can track and passes it to the phase as the duty that scales its ground-tracking update rate. Geometries: <c2/> (the entry state flown two-body with J2, for low-orbit phases), <c3/> (the vehicle at the Moon's position, for the cislunar cruise) and <c4/> (a duty you give). A station change loses <c5/>; the phase's budget gets the longest interval with no station in view and an event gives the duty. Nothing models a network's antennas or schedules.

